# APITable Cursor Rules  
# Repository: apitable/apitable - Open source no-code database platform  
  
## Project Overview  
This is a monorepo for APITable, an open-source alternative to Airtable. It includes a React/Next.js frontend, NestJS room-server, Java Spring Boot backend, and widget system.  
  
## Technology Stack & Architecture  
- **Frontend**: React 18.2.0 + Next.js 12.3.1 + TypeScript 4.8.2  
- **Backend**: NestJS (room-server) + Java Spring Boot (backend-server)    
- **Package Manager**: pnpm 8.6.12 (REQUIRED - enforced by preinstall script)  
- **Build System**: Nx 16.10.0 for monorepo orchestration  
- **Styling**: styled-components 5.3.6 + Antd 4.23.5  
- **Node Version**: 16.15.0 (specified in engines)  
  
## Repository Structure  
apitable/
├── backend-server/ # Java Spring Boot backend
├── packages/
│ ├── ai-components/ # AI-related components
│ ├── components/ # Shared UI components
│ ├── core/ # Core business logic
│ ├── datasheet/ # Main frontend application
│ ├── i18n-lang/ # Internationalization
│ ├── icons/ # Icon components
│ └── widget-sdk/ # Widget development SDK
├── init-db/ # Database initialization
└── package.json # Root package.json

  
## Code Style & Conventions  
  
### TypeScript Conventions  
- **Interfaces**: MUST use "I" prefix (IUnitInfo, IExpression, IStoredData)  
- **Enums**: Use PascalCase or UPPER_CASE for members  
- **Variables**: camelCase, UPPER_CASE, or PascalCase allowed  
- **Parameters**: camelCase or PascalCase, leading underscore allowed  
- **Type-likes**: PascalCase format  
  
### Code Formatting  
- **Indentation**: 2 spaces (enforced by ESLint)  
- **Quotes**: Single quotes preferred  
- **Line Length**: 150 characters maximum  
- **Semicolons**: Required (enforced by @typescript-eslint/semi)  
- **Comma Dangle**: "only-multiline"  
  
### React Conventions  
- Self-closing components enforced for both JSX elements and HTML  
- Display names not required (react/display-name: 0)  
- Hooks rules strictly enforced (react-hooks/rules-of-hooks: "error")  
- Boolean JSX props should omit the value when true  
  
### File Naming & Organization  
- Use camelCase for most files  
- Interface files typically end with .interface.ts  
- Test files use standard Jest conventions  
- Component files should be in PascalCase directories  
  
## Environment Variables & Configuration  
  
### Widget Development  
- Widget visibility controlled via CUSTOM_WIDGET_VISIBLE environment variable  
- Default template URL: WIDGET_DEFAULT_TEMPLATE_URL  
- Widget development help URLs configurable  
- Widget repository prefix configurable via WIDGET_REPO_PREFIX  
  
### Feature Flags  
- Extensive environment variable system for feature toggles  
- Widget-related flags: WIDGET_CENTER_OFFICIAL_TIP_VISIBLE, DASHBOARD_WIDGET_MAX_NUM  
- Security features controlled via SECURITY_* prefixed variables  
- UI features controlled via various *_VISIBLE variables  
  
### Localization  
- Default language: en_US (configurable via SYSTEM_CONFIGURATION_DEFAULT_LANGUAGE)  
- Default theme: dark (configurable via SYSTEM_CONFIGURATION_DEFAULT_THEME)  
- Multi-language support with i18n-lang package  
  
## Development Commands  
  
### Package Management  
- Always use `pnpm` (enforced by preinstall script)  
- Use `pnpm --filter <package>` for package-specific commands  
- Workspace dependencies use `workspace:*` syntax  
  
### Common Scripts  
- `pnpm run sc` - Start core package  
- `pnpm run sd` - Start datasheet in development  
- `pnpm run sr` - Start room-server  
- `pnpm run build:dst` - Build datasheet package  
- `pnpm run lint:fix` - Fix linting issues  
- `pnpm run prettier:fix` - Fix formatting issues  
  
### Testing  
- Use Jest for unit testing  
- Cypress for E2E testing  
- Coverage available for core and room-server packages  
  
## Widget Development Guidelines  
  
### Widget SDK  
- Use @apitable/widget-sdk for widget development  
- Widgets have access to datasheet data through the SDK  
- Maximum widgets per dashboard: 30 (configurable)  
  
### Widget Environment Setup  
- Development help URLs configurable for different stages  
- Browser restriction help documentation available  
- Template source code provided via WIDGET_DEFAULT_TEMPLATE_URL  
  
## Git & Deployment Conventions  
- **Branching**: Gitflow model (develop → feature branches → main)  
- **Commits**: Conventional Commits format required  
- **Versioning**: Semantic Versioning (SemVer)  
- **Changelog**: Keep a Changelog format  
  
## Security & Permissions  
- Row and column level permissions supported  
- Watermark functionality available  
- Audit logging capabilities  
- SAML and SSO support in enterprise versions  
  
## Database & API  
- REST API with full CRUD operations  
- Datasheet Query Language (DQL) for advanced queries  
- Real-time collaboration via WebSocket (room-server)  
- API documentation available via built-in panel  
  
## Styling Guidelines  
- Use styled-components for component styling  
- Antd components for UI library  
- Support for dark/light themes  
- Mobile-responsive design with antd-mobile  
  
## Performance Considerations  
- Canvas rendering engine for smooth spreadsheet interface  
- 100k+ row support with real-time collaboration  
- Operational Transformation (OT) algorithm for concurrent editing  
- Lazy loading and virtualization for large datasets  
  
## Internationalization  
- Use @apitable/i18n-lang package for translations  
- Translation keys should be descriptive  
- Support for multiple locales (en_US, zh_CN, etc.)  
- Community translations via Crowdin  
  
## Error Handling & Logging  
- Sentry integration for error tracking  
- Custom error pages with help links  
- Comprehensive logging in development  
- Production error boundaries  
  
## When Working on This Codebase:  
1. Always run `pnpm install` after cloning  
2. Check environment variables are properly set  
3. Use the provided scripts for consistent development  
4. Follow the established naming conventions strictly  
5. Test widgets in the widget development environment  
6. Ensure responsive design for mobile devices  
7. Consider internationalization for user-facing strings  
8. Use proper TypeScript types and interfaces  
9. Follow the component architecture patterns  
10. Ensure proper error handling and user feedback  
  
## Important Notes:  
- Self-hosted deployment supported with Docker  
- Enterprise features available in hosted version  
- Widget system is highly extensible  
- Real-time collaboration is a core feature  
- API-first design philosophy  
- Strong focus on permissions and security  
